# C09 message page actions — unapplied attach

Issue: https://github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-remote-ops/issues/5
Repo: github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-ios
Base: origin/cursor/c09-message-action-flow-e504 `17f7b4af4e6f5443707158049798022af7835afa`

`NativeChannelMessagePageActions` is the caller the existing channel message page uses for send, edit, recall, and pin. Each method calls `NativeChannelMessageActionEntry` once. A nil port waits. The request id is not rewritten. Blank content is invalid. Outcome stays UNKNOWN. No local receipt store. `appear()` does not send. Search stays on `NativeChannelMessageEntry`. This file does not add a second search chain.

Do not apply this hunk onto `App/AppSession.swift`, `App/AppCompositionRoot.swift`, or `Questify.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj`. Those three files are unchanged in this branch. The SwiftUI page below is also not applied: `NativeChannelMessageActionEntry.swift` and `NativeChannelMessagePageActions.swift` are not in the committed Xcode target, and this change does not edit project.pbxproj. Applying only the view patch would break that target.

XCTest NOT_RUN where swiftc is absent. Not 100%.

## Page patch (not applied)

Existing page: `App/MessagingHistoryView.swift`. No gradient, glow, or emoji icons. The resting layout is unchanged. Appearance calls `appear()` only.

```
diff --git a/App/MessagingHistoryView.swift b/App/MessagingHistoryView.swift
--- a/App/MessagingHistoryView.swift
+++ b/App/MessagingHistoryView.swift
@@ -62,6 +62,7 @@ struct MessagingHistoryView: View {
     @State private var generation: UInt64 = 0
     @State private var visibleMessageID: Int?
     @State private var showingPollComposer = false
+    @State private var channelActions = NativeChannelMessagePageActions()

     init(conversationID: Int, conversation: MessagingConversation? = nil, reader: any MessagingReading, sender:MessageActionCoordinator?=nil,mediaReader:(any SocialMessageMediaReading)?=nil,expanded:IMExpandedNavigationContext?=nil, onConversationMutationAccepted: @escaping (IMScope) -> Void = { _ in }) {
@@ -159,6 +160,7 @@ struct MessagingHistoryView: View {
             // Only a new account epoch or an unfinished first load starts an automatic read.
             if !currentHistoryReady { await reload() }
         }
+        .onAppear { channelActions.appear() }
         .onDisappear { generation &+= 1; isLoadingEarlier = false }
     }
@@ -247,6 +249,46 @@ struct MessagingHistoryView: View {
             && ObjectIdentifier(reader) == source && reader.isConfigured
             && history.conversationID == conversationID
     }
+    func sendChannel(requestID: String?, kind: NotifyKind?, actorID: Int64?, conversationID: Int64?, msgType: Int?, content: String?, extraJSON: String?, replyToID: Int64?, mentionMemberIDs: [Int64] = [], mentionRoleIDs: [Int64] = [], mentionEveryone: Bool = false, port: ImmutableReceiptProducer.ChannelOriginalSend? = nil) throws -> ImmutableReceiptProducer.OriginalReceipt {
+        try channelActions.send(requestID: requestID, kind: kind, actorID: actorID, conversationID: conversationID, msgType: msgType, content: content, extraJSON: extraJSON, replyToID: replyToID, mentionMemberIDs: mentionMemberIDs, mentionRoleIDs: mentionRoleIDs, mentionEveryone: mentionEveryone, port: port)
+    }
+    func editChannel(requestID: String?, kind: NotifyKind?, actorID: Int64?, conversationID: Int64?, messageID: Int64?, content: String?, expectedVersion: Int64?, mentionMemberIDs: [Int64] = [], mentionRoleIDs: [Int64] = [], mentionEveryone: Bool = false, port: ImmutableReceiptProducer.ChannelOriginalEdit? = nil) throws -> ImmutableReceiptProducer.OriginalReceipt {
+        try channelActions.edit(requestID: requestID, kind: kind, actorID: actorID, conversationID: conversationID, messageID: messageID, content: content, expectedVersion: expectedVersion, mentionMemberIDs: mentionMemberIDs, mentionRoleIDs: mentionRoleIDs, mentionEveryone: mentionEveryone, port: port)
+    }
+    func recallChannel(requestID: String?, kind: NotifyKind?, actorID: Int64?, conversationID: Int64?, messageID: Int64?, reason: String?, expectedVersion: Int64?, port: ImmutableReceiptProducer.ChannelOriginalRecall? = nil) throws -> ImmutableReceiptProducer.OriginalReceipt {
+        try channelActions.recall(requestID: requestID, kind: kind, actorID: actorID, conversationID: conversationID, messageID: messageID, reason: reason, expectedVersion: expectedVersion, port: port)
+    }
+    func pinChannel(requestID: String?, kind: NotifyKind?, actorID: Int64?, conversationID: Int64?, messageID: Int64?, pinned: Bool, port: ImmutableReceiptProducer.ChannelOriginalPin? = nil) throws -> ImmutableReceiptProducer.OriginalReceipt {
+        try channelActions.pin(requestID: requestID, kind: kind, actorID: actorID, conversationID: conversationID, messageID: messageID, pinned: pinned, port: port)
+    }
 }
```

`channelActions.send(`, `channelActions.edit(`, `channelActions.recall(`, `channelActions.pin(` each run once per page call. `channelActions.appear()` does not send.

